entry.summary:
tags: powerbi, dax, troubleshooting, tutorial https://pbidocs.com/blog/key-didnt-match-any-rows-error
The full error reads: The key didn't match any rows in the table
This is the opposite problem from a duplicate value error. That one means LOOKUPVALUE() (or a relationship) found too many matching rows. This one means it found zero — the search value you gave it doesn't exist anywhere in the target column. Product Category = LOOKUPVALUE( DimProduct[Category], DimProduct[ProductKey], FactSales[ProductKey] )
Step One: Find Which Values Are Actually Missing Key Exists = Cause 1: A Data Type Mismatch FactSales[ProductKey] = "1001" (text) LOOKUPVALUE searching for "1001" in a column of numbers -> no match Source, {{"ProductKey", Int64.Type}}
) Cause 2: Trailing Whitespace or Case…
